Z||000001||peterh||10-08-1999||01:43 PM||||I was able to replace the rack and pinion on my 86 SE V6 without any special tools, just a combination of wrenches. What are you referring too?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||10-08-1999||03:57 PM||||The fiero inner tie rod ends dont need the special tool. They come out far enough to get them with a wrench. I found this out after buying that tool.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||10-08-1999||10:49 PM||||Peterh, I'm referring to just the inner tie rod ends, not the entire steering rack. Tom, thanks for the insight, if that's true you just saved me a bundle of cash in shop labor charges. Any secret to removing the rubber inner tie rod boots?||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||10-08-1999||11:51 PM||||Yeah cut the clamp and replace it with a big zip tie. Thats who I did mine years ago and they havent moved at all.||||reg||1
